  "id": "transactions-transactions",
  "slug": "transactions",
  "title": "Transactions",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "transactions-in-tasklets",
      "heading": "Transactions in Tasklets",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring Batch ensures data integrity and consistency using Spring-managed transactions, especially during tasklet execution and chunk processing."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Batch/Transactions/Transactions/image.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Transactions/image.png"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 17,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "key-concepts",
      "heading": "Key Concepts",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "The execute() method of a tasklet runs inside a single transaction.",
            "If the tasklet returns RepeatStatus.CONTINUABLE, Spring Batch calls execute again, and each invocation runs in its own new transaction.",
            "You can control transaction behavior (propagation, isolation, timeout) using the transaction-attributes element."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 42,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "example-tasklet",
      "heading": "Example Tasklet",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "java-example",
          "heading": "Java Example",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Component\npublic class SampleTasklet implements Tasklet {\n\n    @Override\n    public RepeatStatus execute(StepContribution contribution, ChunkContext chunkContext) {\n        System.out.println(\"Running inside a transaction...\");\n        return RepeatStatus.FINISHED;\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "xml-with-transaction-attributes",
          "heading": "XML with Transaction Attributes",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<tasklet ref=\"sampleTasklet\">\n    <transaction-attributes propagation=\"REQUIRED\" isolation=\"DEFAULT\" timeout=\"30\"/>\n</tasklet>",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "when-tasklets-use-multiple-transactions",
          "heading": "When Tasklets Use Multiple Transactions",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "return RepeatStatus.CONTINUABLE;",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "This tells Spring Batch:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Run execute() again",
                "Each call = new transaction"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
